/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Deuteronomy chapters 26-30
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("deuteronomy", [
{n:26, name:"Firstfruits and the Tithe", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 26:19",verse:"And to make thee high above all nations which he hath made, in praise, and in name, and in honour; and that thou mayest be an holy people unto the LORD thy God, as he hath spoken."}, facts:["Did you know the firstfruits confession retells Israel's whole story in a few lines, from 'a Syrian ready to perish' to 'a land that floweth with milk and honey' (Deuteronomy 26:5-9)?","Did you know the third-year tithe fed the Levite, the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow, turning an act of worship into provision for the vulnerable (Deuteronomy 26:12)?","Did you know 'peculiar people' in Deuteronomy 26:18 means treasured and set apart, not odd, and the same phrase is later applied to the church (1 Peter 2:9)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where was Israel to bring the firstfruits?", options:["To the place the LORD would choose to place His name","To the threshing floor of each town","To the king's storehouse","To the high place at Bethel"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:2",verse:"That thou shalt take of the first of all the fruit of the earth, which thou shalt bring of thy land that the LORD thy God giveth thee, and shalt put it in a basket, and shalt go unto the place which the LORD thy God shall choose to place his name there.", insight:"Worship has an address; God chooses where He will be met, and His people come to Him there."},
{q:"What was to be put into the basket?", options:["The first of all the fruit of the earth from the land","The best of the cattle","Silver and gold","The firstborn of the flocks"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:2",verse:"That thou shalt take of the first of all the fruit of the earth, which thou shalt bring of thy land that the LORD thy God giveth thee, and shalt put it in a basket, and shalt go unto the place which the LORD thy God shall choose to place his name there.", insight:"First, not last; God gets the beginning of the harvest, not what is left over."},
{q:"What was the offerer to declare to the priest?", options:["I am come unto the country which the LORD sware unto our fathers","I have kept every commandment perfectly","I bring this gift for the poor","I seek forgiveness for my sins"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:3",verse:"And thou shalt go unto the priest that shall be in those days, and say unto him, I profess this day unto the LORD thy God, that I am come unto the country which the LORD sware unto our fathers for to give us.", insight:"Every gift began with a confession of grace; the land was a promise kept, not wages earned."},
{q:"What did the priest do with the basket of firstfruits?", options:["Take it from the offerer's hand and set it before the altar","Burn it with the morning sacrifice","Send it to the king","Divide it among the Levites"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:4",verse:"And the priest shall take the basket out of thine hand, and set it down before the altar of the LORD thy God.", insight:"The priest receives what the people bring; ministry and worship belong together."},
{q:"How did the confession begin?", options:["'A Syrian ready to perish was my father'","'A king of Egypt oppressed us'","'The LORD our God is one'","'In the beginning God created'"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:5",verse:"And thou shalt speak and say before the LORD thy God, A Syrian ready to perish was my father, and he went down into Egypt, and sojourned there with a few, and became there a nation, great, mighty, and populous:", insight:"Israel's story opens with a dying wanderer; God loves to start His nations with nobodies."},
{q:"What happened to the few who went down into Egypt?", options:["They became a nation, great, mighty, and populous","They vanished without a trace","They ruled over Pharaoh","They returned at once to Canaan"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:5",verse:"And thou shalt speak and say before the LORD thy God, A Syrian ready to perish was my father, and he went down into Egypt, and sojourned there with a few, and became there a nation, great, mighty, and populous:", insight:"A few sojourners became a mighty nation; God multiplies what men despise."},
{q:"How did the Egyptians treat Israel?", options:["They evil entreated us, and afflicted us, with hard bondage","They welcomed us as honored guests","They left us alone in Goshen","They paid us fair wages"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:6",verse:"And the Egyptians evil entreated us, and afflicted us, and laid upon us hard bondage:", insight:"The confession names the pain plainly; God does not ask His people to pretty up their suffering."},
{q:"What did the LORD do when Israel cried?", options:["He heard their voice and looked on their affliction","He sent them more work","He waited another generation","He hardened Pharaoh's heart"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:7",verse:"And when we cried unto the LORD God of our fathers, the LORD heard our voice, and looked on our affliction, and our labour, and our oppression:", insight:"Crying out is never wasted; God's ear is tuned to the afflicted."},
{q:"With what did the LORD bring Israel out of Egypt?", options:["With a mighty hand, an outstretched arm, signs, and wonders","With a negotiated treaty","With a bribe of silver","With a secret escape at night"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:8",verse:"And the LORD brought us forth out of Egypt with a mighty hand, and with an outstretched arm, and with great terribleness, and with signs, and with wonders:", insight:"Redemption is God's strong work; no one mistakes the Exodus for diplomacy."},
{q:"To what kind of land did He bring them?", options:["A land that floweth with milk and honey","A land of iron and brass","A desert of hidden wells","A mountain of cedars"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:9",verse:"And he hath brought us into this place, and hath given us this land, even a land that floweth with milk and honey.", insight:"Milk and honey, not bricks and straw; God's destination outshines every bondage."},
{q:"What was the offerer to do after presenting the firstfruits?", options:["Worship before the LORD thy God","Leave the basket and hurry home","Burn the basket with fire","Divide the fruit with the priest"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:10",verse:"And now, behold, I have brought the firstfruits of the land, which thou, O LORD, hast given me. And thou shalt set it before the LORD thy God, and worship before the LORD thy God:", insight:"The gift ends in worship, not transaction; the basket is laid down and the heart bows lower."},
{q:"Who was to share in the rejoicing over the harvest?", options:["The offerer, the Levite, and the stranger","Only the priests","Only the man's own family","The king and his court"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:11",verse:"And thou shalt rejoice in every good thing which the LORD thy God hath given unto thee, and unto thine house, thou, and the Levite, and the stranger that is among you.", insight:"Joy in God's goodness is meant to be shared, especially with those who have no harvest of their own."},
{q:"Who received the tithe in the third year?", options:["The Levite, the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow","The elders of the city","The king's treasury","The soldiers of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:12",verse:"When thou hast made an end of tithing all the tithes of thine increase the third year, which is the year of tithing, and hast given it unto the Levite, the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow, that they may eat within thy gates, and be filled;", insight:"Every third year, worship fed the vulnerable; a generous heart is part of true religion."},
{q:"What did the tithe-giver confess about the hallowed things?", options:["I have brought away the hallowed things out of mine house","I have hidden them in my field","I have sold them for silver","I have kept them for my children"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:13",verse:"Then thou shalt say before the LORD thy God, I have brought away the hallowed things out of mine house, and also have given them unto the Levite, and unto the stranger, to the fatherless, and to the widow, according to all thy commandments which thou hast commanded me: I have not transgressed thy commandments, neither have I forgotten them:", insight:"Holiness meant parting with what was precious; the hallowed things left the house, not stayed in it."},
{q:"What did the man declare he had NOT done with the tithe?", options:["Eaten it in mourning, used it uncleanly, or given it for the dead","Shared it with his neighbor","Counted it carefully","Brought it to the priest"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:14",verse:"I have not eaten thereof in my mourning, neither have I taken away ought thereof for any unclean use, nor given ought thereof for the dead: but I have hearkened to the voice of the LORD my God, and have done according to all that thou hast commanded me.", insight:"The tithe was handled with clean hands and a clear conscience; sacred things demand honest dealing."},
{q:"What did the prayer ask God to do from heaven?", options:["Look down from thy holy habitation and bless thy people Israel","Send fire upon the altar","Rain manna again","Strike the enemies"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:15",verse:"Look down from thy holy habitation, from heaven, and bless thy people Israel, and the land which thou hast given us, as thou swarest unto our fathers, a land that floweth with milk and honey.", insight:"After obedience comes bold asking; the faithful may pray heaven's blessing down on the land."},
{q:"When did Moses say the LORD commanded these statutes?", options:["This day","In the days of Abraham","At Mount Sinai only","In the fortieth year"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:16",verse:"This day the LORD thy God hath commanded thee to do these statutes and judgments: thou shalt therefore keep and do them with all thine heart, and with all thy soul.", insight:"God's commands are always 'this day'; obedience is never a yesterday matter."},
{q:"What had Israel 'avouched' the LORD to be that day?", options:["Their God, whose ways they would walk in","Their judge only in wartime","A distant creator","One god among many"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:17",verse:"Thou hast avouched the LORD this day to be thy God, and to walk in his ways, and to keep his statutes, and his commandments, and his judgments, and to hearken unto his voice:", insight:"'Avouch' is covenant language; Israel publicly owned the LORD as theirs, and His ways as their path."},
{q:"What had the LORD 'avouched' Israel to be?", options:["His peculiar people, to keep all His commandments","A nation like all others","His servants for a season","A forgotten tribe"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:18",verse:"And the LORD hath avouched thee this day to be his peculiar people, as he hath promised thee, and that thou shouldest keep all his commandments;", insight:"Peculiar means treasured and set apart; God claims His people as His own special possession."},
{q:"What did the LORD promise to make Israel?", options:["High above all nations, in praise, in name, and in honour","Rich above all merchants","Mighty above all armies","Wise above all scholars"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 26:19",verse:"And to make thee high above all nations which he hath made, in praise, and in name, and in honour; and that thou mayest be an holy people unto the LORD thy God, as he hath spoken.", insight:"Exaltation follows consecration; God lifts high the people who are holy to Him."}
]},
{n:27, name:"The Altar on Ebal", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 27:26",verse:"Cursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this law to do them. And all the people shall say, Amen."}, facts:["Did you know Gerizim and Ebal face each other across the valley of Shechem, so the blessing and the curse were proclaimed within hearing of all Israel (Deuteronomy 27:12-14)?","Did you know the altar at Ebal had to be built of whole stones with no iron tool lifted on them, keeping God's altar free from human carving (Deuteronomy 27:5-6)?","Did you know there are twelve curses in Deuteronomy 27, and after each one the whole congregation answered 'Amen' (Deuteronomy 27:15-26)?"], questions:[
{q:"What was Israel to set up on the day they crossed the Jordan?", options:["Great stones, plaistered with plaister","An altar of gold","A bronze serpent","A pillar of cloud"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:2",verse:"And it shall be on the day when ye shall pass over Jordan unto the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee, that thou shalt set thee up great stones, and plaister them with plaister:", insight:"Before the battles came the monument; God's law would stand in stone at the border of promise."},
{q:"What was to be written on the stones?", options:["All the words of this law","The names of the twelve tribes","The song of Moses","The census of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:3",verse:"And thou shalt write upon them all the words of this law, when thou art passed over, that thou mayest go in unto the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee, a land that floweth with milk and honey; as the LORD God of thy fathers hath promised thee.", insight:"The law was published in stone for all to read; God's word was never meant to be hidden."},
{q:"Where were the stones to be set up?", options:["In mount Ebal","On Mount Gerizim","In the Jordan river","At Gilgal"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:4",verse:"Therefore it shall be when ye be gone over Jordan, that ye shall set up these stones, which I command you this day, in mount Ebal, and thou shalt plaister them with plaister.", insight:"Ebal, the mount of cursing, would carry the written law; the warning and the word stand together."},
{q:"What was forbidden on the altar stones?", options:["Lifting any iron tool upon them","Burning incense","Building it higher than a man","Using them after sunset"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:5",verse:"And there shalt thou build an altar unto the LORD thy God, an altar of stones: thou shalt not lift up any iron tool upon them.", insight:"No human tool was to shape God's altar; worship must not bear the marks of man's carving."},
{q:"What kind of stones were to build the altar?", options:["Whole stones","Polished marble","Stones of equal size","Stones from the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:6",verse:"Thou shalt build the altar of the LORD thy God of whole stones: and thou shalt offer burnt offerings thereon unto the LORD thy God:", insight:"Whole, untouched stones; God accepts what He has made, not what we have manufactured."},
{q:"What offerings were to be made at Ebal, and what followed?", options:["Peace offerings, then eating and rejoicing before the LORD","Burnt offerings only, then silence","Sin offerings, then fasting","No offerings, only prayer"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:7",verse:"And thou shalt offer peace offerings, and shalt eat there, and rejoice before the LORD thy God.", insight:"Even on the mount of cursing, God spreads a feast; judgment pronounced and joy shared at the same altar."},
{q:"How were the words of the law to be written?", options:["Very plainly","In the tongue of Egypt","In sealed scrolls","In poetry"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:8",verse:"And thou shalt write upon the stones all the words of this law very plainly.", insight:"Very plainly; God's law is not a riddle for scholars but a signpost for the people."},
{q:"What did Moses declare to Israel that day?", options:["This day thou art become the people of the LORD thy God","This day thou art free from the law","This day thou art greater than Egypt","This day thou art alone in the land"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:9",verse:"And Moses and the priests the Levites spake unto all Israel, saying, Take heed, and hearken, O Israel; this day thou art become the people of the LORD thy God.", insight:"Covenant day was identity day; before the land came the belonging."},
{q:"Which six tribes stood on Mount Gerizim to bless?", options:["Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Joseph, and Benjamin","Reuben, Gad, Asher, Zebulun, Dan, Naphtali","The priests and Levites only","The elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:12",verse:"These shall stand upon mount Gerizim to bless the people, when ye are come over Jordan; Simeon, and Levi, and Judah, and Issachar, and Joseph, and Benjamin:", insight:"Six tribes on the mount of blessing, facing six on the mount of cursing; the whole nation stood in the valley between."},
{q:"Which six tribes stood on Mount Ebal for the curse?", options:["Reuben, Gad, Asher, Zebulun, Dan, and Naphtali","Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Joseph, Benjamin","The mixed multitude","The warriors only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:13",verse:"And these shall stand upon mount Ebal to curse; Reuben, Gad, and Asher, and Zebulun, Dan, and Naphtali.", insight:"Every tribe had its place in the solemn ceremony; no one watched from a distance."},
{q:"Who pronounced the curses, and how?", options:["The Levites, with a loud voice","Moses, in a whisper","The elders, in song","The priests, with trumpets"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:14",verse:"And the Levites shall speak, and say unto all the men of Israel with a loud voice,", insight:"With a loud voice; the curses were not muttered but proclaimed, so every ear would hear."},
{q:"Who was cursed first?", options:["The man that maketh any graven or molten image","The thief","The murderer","The false witness"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:15",verse:"Cursed be the man that maketh any graven or molten image, an abomination unto the LORD, the work of the hands of the craftsman, and putteth it in a secret place. And all the people shall answer and say, Amen.", insight:"Idolatry heads the list; a carved god is the first step away from the living God."},
{q:"After each curse, what did all the people answer?", options:["Amen","A song of praise","Nothing","Hosanna"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:15",verse:"Cursed be the man that maketh any graven or molten image, an abomination unto the LORD, the work of the hands of the craftsman, and putteth it in a secret place. And all the people shall answer and say, Amen.", insight:"'Amen' means 'so be it'; the people bound themselves to every verdict with their own mouths."},
{q:"Who was cursed for moving a boundary?", options:["He that removeth his neighbour's landmark","He that builds a high wall","He that digs a deep well","He that plants a vineyard"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:17",verse:"Cursed be he that removeth his neighbour’s landmark. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"Stealing land by night is theft in God's eyes; ancient boundaries carry His protection."},
{q:"Who was cursed for misleading the vulnerable?", options:["He that maketh the blind to wander out of the way","He that ignores the poor","He that taxes the widow","He that hires the stranger"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:18",verse:"Cursed be he that maketh the blind to wander out of the way. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"Misleading the blind is cruelty dressed as guidance; God defends those who cannot see the trap."},
{q:"Whose judgment was not to be perverted?", options:["The stranger, the fatherless, and the widow","The king and his princes","The priests","The rich landowners"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:19",verse:"Cursed be he that perverteth the judgment of the stranger, fatherless, and widow. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"The three with no protector get God's protection; perverting their justice invites His curse."},
{q:"Which sin of the household was cursed?", options:["Lying with his father's wife","Marrying a foreign wife","Divorcing without cause","Withholding an inheritance"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:20",verse:"Cursed be he that lieth with his father’s wife; because he uncovereth his father’s skirt. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"Uncovering a father's nakedness breaks the family at its root; some boundaries guard the home itself."},
{q:"Who was cursed for secret violence?", options:["He that smiteth his neighbour secretly","He that speaks in anger","He that challenges to battle","He that flees from war"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:24",verse:"Cursed be he that smiteth his neighbour secretly. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"Secret blows are still seen; the curse reaches the violence no witness can prove."},
{q:"Who was cursed for killing for hire?", options:["He that taketh reward to slay an innocent person","He that serves as a soldier","He that executes a criminal","He that defends his home"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:25",verse:"Cursed be he that taketh reward to slay an innocent person. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"Blood money turns murder into merchandise; God curses the trade in innocent life."},
{q:"What was the final, crowning curse?", options:["Cursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this law to do them","Cursed be he that leaves the land","Cursed be he that doubts the prophets","Cursed be he that fears the enemy"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 27:26",verse:"Cursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this law to do them. And all the people shall say, Amen.", insight:"The last curse gathers up all the rest; it is not partial obedience but the whole law that God requires."}
]},
{n:28, name:"Blessings and Curses", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 28:2",verse:"And all these blessings shall come on thee, and overtake thee, if thou shalt hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God."}, facts:["Did you know the blessings and the curses are mirror images, the same city, field, basket, and store blessed in verses 3-6 and cursed in verses 16-19 (Deuteronomy 28:3-19)?","Did you know 'the head, and not the tail' promised Israel leadership among the nations, not merely personal success (Deuteronomy 28:13)?","Did you know Moses said the curses would come 'because thou servedst not the LORD thy God with joyfulness,' making a glad heart the true safeguard (Deuteronomy 28:47)?"], questions:[
{q:"What would the LORD do for Israel if they diligently obeyed?", options:["Set them on high above all nations of the earth","Give them Egypt's throne","Make them invisible to enemies","Grant them endless gold"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:1",verse:"And it shall come to pass, if thou shalt hearken diligently unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to observe and to do all his commandments which I command thee this day, that the LORD thy God will set thee on high above all nations of the earth:", insight:"Obedience lifts a nation; God sets high those who stoop to keep His word."},
{q:"What would the blessings do?", options:["Come on thee, and overtake thee","Trickle down over many years","Come only to the priests","Wait in heaven"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:2",verse:"And all these blessings shall come on thee, and overtake thee, if thou shalt hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God.", insight:"Blessings that overtake you; obedience turns God's favor into a pursuer."},
{q:"Where would Israel be blessed?", options:["In the city, and in the field","In the temple only","In foreign lands only","In their dreams"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:3",verse:"Blessed shalt thou be in the city, and blessed shalt thou be in the field.", insight:"City and field, town and farm; no corner of life lies outside God's blessing."},
{q:"What three fruits would be blessed?", options:["The fruit of thy body, thy ground, and thy cattle","The fruit of thy orchards, vines, and olives","Thy sons, thy servants, and thy strangers","Thy wheat, thy wine, and thy oil"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:4",verse:"Blessed shall be the fruit of thy body, and the fruit of thy ground, and the fruit of thy cattle, the increase of thy kine, and the flocks of thy sheep.", insight:"Children, crops, and herds; God blesses the family, the farm, and the flock."},
{q:"When would Israel be blessed?", options:["When thou comest in, and when thou goest out","Only on feast days","Only in wartime","Only in old age"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:6",verse:"Blessed shalt thou be when thou comest in, and blessed shalt thou be when thou goest out.", insight:"Coming and going, the rhythm of daily life; blessing covers the doorway both ways."},
{q:"How would Israel's enemies flee?", options:["They would come one way and flee seven ways","They would flee to Egypt","They would surrender at once","They would never come at all"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:7",verse:"The LORD shall cause thine enemies that rise up against thee to be smitten before thy face: they shall come out against thee one way, and flee before thee seven ways.", insight:"One way in, seven ways out; God scatters the enemies of the obedient."},
{q:"What would all the peoples of the earth see and feel?", options:["That Israel is called by the name of the LORD, and be afraid","Israel's great wealth, and envy it","Israel's armies, and join them","Israel's wisdom, and copy it"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:10",verse:"And all people of the earth shall see that thou art called by the name of the LORD; and they shall be afraid of thee.", insight:"God's name on a people is their true defense; nations fear what heaven has marked."},
{q:"What would Israel do with many nations?", options:["Lend unto many nations, and not borrow","Conquer many nations","Trade only with Egypt","Refuse all foreign dealings"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:12",verse:"The LORD shall open unto thee his good treasure, the heaven to give the rain unto thy land in his season, and to bless all the work of thine hand: and thou shalt lend unto many nations, and thou shalt not borrow.", insight:"The lender leads; God meant His people's prosperity to serve the nations, not be enslaved by them."},
{q:"What would Israel be among the nations?", options:["The head, and not the tail; above only, and not beneath","The sword, and not the shield","The first in war, and the last in peace","The richest in gold, and the poorest in silver"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:13",verse:"And the LORD shall make thee the head, and not the tail; and thou shalt be above only, and thou shalt not be beneath; if that thou hearken unto the commandments of the LORD thy God, which I command thee this day, to observe and to do them:", insight:"Head, not tail; obedience was meant to make Israel the leader, not the follower, of nations."},
{q:"Why would the curses come upon Israel?", options:["Because they served not the LORD with joyfulness and gladness of heart","Because they were too few","Because they lacked weapons","Because they forgot the feasts"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:47",verse:"Because thou servedst not the LORD thy God with joyfulness, and with gladness of heart, for the abundance of all things;", insight:"Joyless service invites judgment; God wants glad hearts, not grudging hands."},
{q:"What would the curses do if Israel disobeyed?", options:["Come upon thee, and overtake thee","Threaten from afar","Fall on the neighbors","Wait for the next generation"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:15",verse:"But it shall come to pass, if thou wilt not hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to observe to do all his commandments and his statutes which I command thee this day; that all these curses shall come upon thee, and overtake thee:", insight:"Curses overtake like blessings do; disobedience is pursued just as surely as obedience is rewarded."},
{q:"What would the heavens and earth become?", options:["The heaven brass, and the earth iron","The heaven dark, and the earth flooded","The heaven silent, and the earth barren","The heaven red, and the earth cracked"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:23",verse:"And thy heaven that is over thy head shall be brass, and the earth that is under thee shall be iron.", insight:"Brass skies and iron earth; when God shuts the heavens, the ground turns to metal."},
{q:"What would the rain of the land become?", options:["Powder and dust","Blood and fire","Hail and snow","Worms and locusts"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:24",verse:"The LORD shall make the rain of thy land powder and dust: from heaven shall it come down upon thee, until thou be destroyed.", insight:"Dust for rain; the curse turns heaven's gift into the desert's scourge."},
{q:"With what would the LORD smite them?", options:["With madness, and blindness, and astonishment of heart","With famine only","With plague only","With drought only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:28",verse:"The LORD shall smite thee with madness, and blindness, and astonishment of heart:", insight:"Madness, blindness, astonishment; disobedience darkens the mind before it ruins the land."},
{q:"What losses are named in the curse?", options:["Betroth a wife another shall take; build a house another shall dwell in","Lose thy flocks and thy fields","Lose thy sons in battle","Lose thy name among the tribes"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:30",verse:"Thou shalt betroth a wife, and another man shall lie with her: thou shalt build an house, and thou shalt not dwell therein: thou shalt plant a vineyard, and shalt not gather the grapes thereof.", insight:"The curse strikes at home and hope; another enjoys what your hands have built."},
{q:"What would happen to their sons and daughters?", options:["Given unto another people, with eyes looking and failing","Sent to Egypt as slaves","Scattered to the islands","Taken by the priests"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:32",verse:"Thy sons and thy daughters shall be given unto another people, and thine eyes shall look, and fail with longing for them all the day long: and there shall be no might in thine hand.", insight:"Children given away while parents watch helplessly; there is no deeper wound than this."},
{q:"How would the invading nation come?", options:["From far, swift as the eagle flieth","Slowly, over many years","By sea in small boats","Through the desert on foot"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:49",verse:"The LORD shall bring a nation against thee from far, from the end of the earth, as swift as the eagle flieth; a nation whose tongue thou shalt not understand;", insight:"Swift as the eagle; judgment, when it comes, does not crawl."},
{q:"Where would the LORD scatter them?", options:["Among all people, from one end of the earth to the other","To Egypt only","To the wilderness only","To the islands only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:64",verse:"And the LORD shall scatter thee among all people, from the one end of the earth even unto the other; and there thou shalt serve other gods, which neither thou nor thy fathers have known, even wood and stone.", insight:"From end to end of the earth; the scattering matches the wideness of the disobedience."},
{q:"What rest would they find among the nations?", options:["No ease, but a trembling heart, failing eyes, and sorrow of mind","Peace and safety","Wealth and honor","Forgetfulness of home"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:65",verse:"And among these nations shalt thou find no ease, neither shall the sole of thy foot have rest: but the LORD shall give thee there a trembling heart, and failing of eyes, and sorrow of mind:", insight:"No ease for the exiled heart; distance from God makes every resting place a wilderness."},
{q:"How would the LORD bring them back to Egypt?", options:["With ships, to be sold unto enemies, and no man shall buy","On foot through the desert","In chains of brass","By the hand of Pharaoh"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 28:68",verse:"And the LORD shall bring thee into Egypt again with ships, by the way whereof I spake unto thee, Thou shalt see it no more again: and there ye shall be sold unto your enemies for bondmen and bondwomen, and no man shall buy you.", insight:"Back to Egypt by ship, unsold even as slaves; the curse completes the circle of bondage."}
]},
{n:29, name:"The Covenant in Moab", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 29:29",verse:"The secret things belong unto the LORD our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law."}, facts:["Did you know this covenant was made with those 'that is not here with us this day,' binding generations not yet born (Deuteronomy 29:14-15)?","Did you know Moses warned of 'a root that beareth gall and wormwood,' a picture of hidden bitterness spreading through a whole community (Deuteronomy 29:18)?","Did you know Deuteronomy 29:29 draws the line between secret things, which belong to God, and revealed things, which belong to us and our children forever?"], questions:[
{q:"Where was this covenant made?", options:["In the land of Moab, beside the covenant made in Horeb","In Egypt","At Mount Gerizim","In the wilderness of Zin"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:1",verse:"These are the words of the covenant, which the LORD commanded Moses to make with the children of Israel in the land of Moab, beside the covenant which he made with them in Horeb.", insight:"Moab, on the edge of promise; a new generation makes its own covenant before crossing over."},
{q:"What had Israel's eyes seen?", options:["Great temptations, signs, and great miracles","The tablets of stone","The ark of the covenant","The promised land"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:3",verse:"The great temptations which thine eyes have seen, the signs, and those great miracles:", insight:"They had seen signs and miracles; memory of God's wonders is the ground of covenant."},
{q:"What had the LORD not yet given them?", options:["An heart to perceive, eyes to see, and ears to hear, unto this day","The land of Canaan","The ten commandments","A king to rule them"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:4",verse:"Yet the LORD hath not given you an heart to perceive, and eyes to see, and ears to hear, unto this day.", insight:"Seeing is not perceiving; God must give the heart that understands what the eyes have seen."},
{q:"What did not wear out in forty years?", options:["Their clothes, and their shoes","Their tents","Their weapons","Their weapons of war"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:5",verse:"And I have led you forty years in the wilderness: your clothes are not waxen old upon you, and thy shoe is not waxen old upon thy foot.", insight:"Forty years, and clothes not worn out; God's provision outlasts the wilderness."},
{q:"Why had they not eaten bread or drunk wine?", options:["That they might know that He is the LORD their God","Because there was none to buy","Because it was forbidden forever","Because they were fasting"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:6",verse:"Ye have not eaten bread, neither have ye drunk wine or strong drink: that ye might know that I am the LORD your God.", insight:"Manna instead of bread, that they might know Him; God sometimes removes the ordinary to reveal Himself."},
{q:"Which two kings came out against them?", options:["Sihon king of Heshbon, and Og king of Bashan","Pharaoh and Abimelech","Balak and Balaam","The kings of Canaan"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:7",verse:"And when ye came unto this place, Sihon the king of Heshbon, and Og the king of Bashan, came out against us unto battle, and we smote them:", insight:"Sihon and Og fell before Israel entered Canaan; God gives victories before the promise to build faith for it."},
{q:"Who received the conquered land east of Jordan?", options:["The Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh","The Levites","The mixed multitude","The elders"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:8",verse:"And we took their land, and gave it for an inheritance unto the Reubenites, and to the Gadites, and to the half tribe of Manasseh.", insight:"Two and a half tribes settled east of Jordan; God's gifts come in the order He chooses, not the order we expect."},
{q:"Who stood before the LORD that day?", options:["Captains, tribes, elders, and officers, all of Israel","Moses alone","The priests only","The warriors"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:10",verse:"Ye stand this day all of you before the LORD your God; your captains of your tribes, your elders, and your officers, with all the men of Israel,", insight:"All of you; covenant is not made by representatives alone but by the whole people standing together."},
{q:"Who else was included, down to the lowest?", options:["Little ones, wives, the stranger, the hewer of wood and drawer of water","Only the firstborn sons","Only the free men","Only those over twenty"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:11",verse:"Your little ones, your wives, and thy stranger that is in thy camp, from the hewer of thy wood unto the drawer of thy water:", insight:"From the hewer of wood to the drawer of water; no one is too low to stand in covenant with God."},
{q:"With whom else was the covenant made?", options:["With him that is not here with us this day","With the Egyptians","With the Moabites","With the angels"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:15",verse:"But with him that standeth here with us this day before the LORD our God, and also with him that is not here with us this day:", insight:"With those not yet born; covenant reaches forward, binding generations still to come."},
{q:"What had Israel seen among the nations?", options:["Their abominations, idols of wood and stone, silver and gold","Their great armies","Their walled cities","Their harvest festivals"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:17",verse:"And ye have seen their abominations, and their idols, wood and stone, silver and gold, which were among them:)", insight:"Wood, stone, silver, gold; the idols of the nations are expensive and empty."},
{q:"What dangerous 'root' might grow among them?", options:["A root that beareth gall and wormwood","A root of pride","A root of wealth","A root of fear"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:18",verse:"Lest there should be among you man, or woman, or family, or tribe, whose heart turneth away this day from the LORD our God, to go and serve the gods of these nations; lest there should be among you a root that beareth gall and wormwood;", insight:"Gall and wormwood, bitterness in the root; one person's turning away can poison the whole field."},
{q:"What would the presumptuous man say in his heart?", options:["I shall have peace, though I walk in the imagination of mine heart","God will never judge","The law is too hard","The prophets are liars"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:19",verse:"And it come to pass, when he heareth the words of this curse, that he bless himself in his heart, saying, I shall have peace, though I walk in the imagination of mine heart, to add drunkenness to thirst:", insight:"Self-blessed peace while walking in stubbornness; presumption calls God's curse a blessing."},
{q:"What would the LORD not do for that man?", options:["Spare him; His anger and jealousy would smoke against him","Hear his prayers","Send him prophets","Give him children"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:20",verse:"The LORD will not spare him, but then the anger of the LORD and his jealousy shall smoke against that man, and all the curses that are written in this book shall lie upon him, and the LORD shall blot out his name from under heaven.", insight:"God will not spare the defiant; jealousy is love's fire turned against betrayal."},
{q:"Who would one day see the plagues of the land?", options:["The generations to come, and the stranger from a far land","The Egyptians","The Canaanites","The priests"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:22",verse:"So that the generation to come of your children that shall rise up after you, and the stranger that shall come from a far land, shall say, when they see the plagues of that land, and the sicknesses which the LORD hath laid upon it;", insight:"Future generations and far strangers would read the ruins; judgment leaves a testimony."},
{q:"What would the cursed land look like?", options:["Brimstone, salt, and burning, like the overthrow of Sodom","A fruitful garden","A pleasant wilderness","A land of rivers"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:23",verse:"And that the whole land thereof is brimstone, and salt, and burning, that it is not sown, nor beareth, nor any grass groweth therein, like the overthrow of Sodom, and Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboim, which the LORD overthrew in his anger, and in his wrath:", insight:"Like Sodom; the land itself would preach what happens when covenant is broken."},
{q:"What would the nations ask?", options:["Wherefore hath the LORD done thus unto this land?","Who is the LORD?","Where is Israel's God?","What are these stones?"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:24",verse:"Even all nations shall say, Wherefore hath the LORD done thus unto this land? what meaneth the heat of this great anger?", insight:"The nations would ask why; God's judgments are meant to be noticed and questioned."},
{q:"What answer would be given?", options:["Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD God of their fathers","Because they were weak","Because their enemies were strong","Because the land was poor"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:25",verse:"Then men shall say, Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD God of their fathers, which he made with them when he brought them forth out of the land of Egypt:", insight:"Forsaken the covenant; the answer to every 'why' of judgment is the broken promise."},
{q:"What had they done?", options:["Gone and served other gods, and worshipped them","Forgotten the feasts","Neglected the sabbath","Despised the priests"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:26",verse:"For they went and served other gods, and worshipped them, gods whom they knew not, and whom he had not given unto them:", insight:"They served gods they had not known; novelty in worship is often just old idolatry."},
{q:"What belongs to us and our children forever?", options:["The things which are revealed","The secret things","The hidden counsels","The unwritten laws"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 29:29",verse:"The secret things belong unto the LORD our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law.", insight:"Secret things belong to God; revealed things belong to us. Obey what He has shown, and trust Him with the rest."}
]},
{n:30, name:"Choose Life", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 30:19",verse:"I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live:"}, facts:["Did you know Deuteronomy 30:6 promises that God Himself will circumcise hearts, turning the command to love Him into His own gift (Deuteronomy 30:6)?","Did you know Moses argued the commandment is 'not in heaven' and 'neither beyond the sea' but 'very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart' (Deuteronomy 30:11-14)?","Did you know 'choose life' is spoken with heaven and earth called as witnesses, making it the most solemn invitation in the Torah (Deuteronomy 30:19)?"], questions:[
{q:"What would Israel do among the nations where they were driven?", options:["Call to mind the blessing and the curse","Forget the law entirely","Build new altars","Curse their enemies"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:1",verse:"And it shall come to pass, when all these things are come upon thee, the blessing and the curse, which I have set before thee, and thou shalt call them to mind among all the nations, whither the LORD thy God hath driven thee,", insight:"Exile would become a school; remembering God's word in a far land is the first step home."},
{q:"What would returning to the LORD require?", options:["Obeying His voice with all the heart and all the soul","A burnt offering only","A new king","A journey to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:2",verse:"And shalt return unto the LORD thy God, and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart, and with all thy soul;", insight:"With all the heart and all the soul; half-hearted return gets a half-hearted welcome."},
{q:"What would the LORD do for the returning?", options:["Turn their captivity, have compassion, and gather them from all nations","Leave them in exile","Send them to Egypt","Forget their sins only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:3",verse:"That then the LORD thy God will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither the LORD thy God hath scattered thee.", insight:"Compassion moves Him to gather; God's mercy does not wait for us to find our own way home."},
{q:"How far would His gathering reach?", options:["To the outmost parts of heaven","To the nearest city","To the Jordan river","To the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:4",verse:"If any of thine be driven out unto the outmost parts of heaven, from thence will the LORD thy God gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:", insight:"To the outmost parts of heaven; no distance is too far for the God who gathers."},
{q:"What would He do for them beyond their fathers?", options:["Do them good, and multiply them above their fathers","Give them Egypt's land","Make them immortal","Give them new laws"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:5",verse:"And the LORD thy God will bring thee into the land which thy fathers possessed, and thou shalt possess it; and he will do thee good, and multiply thee above thy fathers.", insight:"Above their fathers; restoration in God's hands outdoes the original blessing."},
{q:"What would the LORD do to their hearts?", options:["Circumcise their hearts, to love the LORD with all the heart","Harden their hearts","Take away their hearts","Write the law on stone again"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:6",verse:"And the LORD thy God will circumcise thine heart, and the heart of thy seed, to love the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, that thou mayest live.", insight:"God circumcises the heart Himself; the love He commands, He also creates."},
{q:"Where would He put the curses?", options:["Upon their enemies, and on them that hate them","Upon the land","Upon the cattle","Upon the strangers"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:7",verse:"And the LORD thy God will put all these curses upon thine enemies, and on them that hate thee, which persecuted thee.", insight:"The curses move from Israel to her enemies; God turns the weapons of judgment around."},
{q:"What would the returned people do?", options:["Return and obey the voice of the LORD, and do His commandments","Build a new temple","Choose a new leader","Offer sacrifices only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:8",verse:"And thou shalt return and obey the voice of the LORD, and do all his commandments which I command thee this day.", insight:"Return and obey; true repentance always walks back onto the path of the commandments."},
{q:"In what would the LORD make them plenteous?", options:["In every work of their hand","In silver only","In cattle only","In children only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:9",verse:"And the LORD thy God will make thee plenteous in every work of thine hand, in the fruit of thy body, and in the fruit of thy cattle, and in the fruit of thy land, for good: for the LORD will again rejoice over thee for good, as he rejoiced over thy fathers:", insight:"Every work of their hand; God's blessing touches the labor, not just the leisure."},
{q:"How is the commandment described?", options:["Not hidden, neither far off","Hidden in heaven","Far beyond the sea","Too hard to keep"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:11",verse:"For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off.", insight:"Not hidden, not far off; God's word is near because He wants to be obeyed, not admired from afar."},
{q:"What need no one say about the commandment?", options:["Who shall go up for us to heaven, to bring it unto us","Who shall open the sealed book","Who shall climb the mountain","Who shall cross the desert"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:12",verse:"It is not in heaven, that thou shouldest say, Who shall go up for us to heaven, and bring it unto us, that we may hear it, and do it?", insight:"No need to climb to heaven; the word has already come down to us."},
{q:"What need no one say about fetching it?", options:["Who shall go over the sea for us, and bring it unto us","Who shall sail to Tarshish","Who shall dive to the deep","Who shall cross the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:13",verse:"Neither is it beyond the sea, that thou shouldest say, Who shall go over the sea for us, and bring it unto us, that we may hear it, and do it?", insight:"No voyage needed; obedience is not an expedition but a decision."},
{q:"Where is the word?", options:["Very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart","In the ark only","In the priest's keeping","In the book of the law only"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:14",verse:"But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it.", insight:"In your mouth and in your heart; God's word lives where you speak and where you love."},
{q:"What did Moses set before them that day?", options:["Life and good, and death and evil","Blessing only","Curse only","Peace and war"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:15",verse:"See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil;", insight:"Life and good, death and evil; Moses lays the two roads side by side and lets them see."},
{q:"What did Moses command them to do?", options:["Love the LORD thy God, walk in His ways, keep His commandments","Fear the nations","Build high walls","Number the people"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:16",verse:"In that I command thee this day to love the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live and multiply: and the LORD thy God shall bless thee in the land whither thou goest to possess it.", insight:"Love, walk, keep; the command is a relationship, a road, and a rule, all at once."},
{q:"What would happen if their heart turned away?", options:["They would be drawn away to worship other gods","They would prosper anyway","God would overlook it","The priests would intervene"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:17",verse:"But if thine heart turn away, so that thou wilt not hear, but shalt be drawn away, and worship other gods, and serve them;", insight:"A turned heart drifts; no one falls into idolatry all at once, but by turning away first."},
{q:"What did Moses denounce that day?", options:["That ye shall surely perish","That the land would fail","That the temple would fall","That the king would die"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:18",verse:"I denounce unto you this day, that ye shall surely perish, and that ye shall not prolong your days upon the land, whither thou passest over Jordan to go to possess it.", insight:"'I denounce unto you'; Moses speaks plainly because he loves them too much to soften the warning."},
{q:"What had Moses set before them that day?", options:["Life and good, and death and evil","Blessing only, with no curse","Wealth and poverty","War and peace"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:15",verse:"See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil;", insight:"Life and good, death and evil; God never hides the stakes of our choices."},
{q:"What did Moses urge them to choose, and why?", options:["Choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live","Choose riches, that thou mayest prosper","Choose peace, that thou mayest rest","Choose wisdom, that thou mayest lead"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:19",verse:"I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live:", insight:"Choose life, for your children's sake too; our choices today are our seed's inheritance tomorrow."},
{q:"Why cleave unto the LORD?", options:["For He is thy life, and the length of thy days","For He gives wealth","For He defeats enemies","For He sends rain"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 30:20",verse:"That thou mayest love the LORD thy God, and that thou mayest obey his voice, and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land which the LORD sware unto thy fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, to give them.", insight:"He is thy life; God is not the means to life, He is life itself."}
]}
]);
